Description: several WhatsApp accounts at the same time
 Palabre shows several WhatsApp Web accounts at the same time, each one in
 its own isolated web session (separate cookies and storage), logged in with
 a QR code and kept logged in between launches.
 .
 Accounts can be displayed side by side in a grid, in tabs, or one window per
 account; any account can be detached into its own window and attached back
 without reloading the page.
 .
 Each account has a name and a color, an unread message badge and its own
 desktop notifications. Palabre also offers a system tray icon, a badge on the
 dock icon, start with the session, keyboard shortcuts, per-account zoom, a
 do-not-disturb mode and a privacy blur.
 .
 It uses WebKitGTK 6.0, GTK 4 and libadwaita from Ubuntu, and installs an
 AppArmor profile so that the WebKit sandbox works on Ubuntu 24.04.
 .
 The package depends on mawena-depot, the signed APT repository of its
 author (https://apt.mawena.cloud), so "apt upgrade" keeps Palabre up to date.
 .
 Palabre is not affiliated with WhatsApp or Meta.

